      en: "The Kambar-Ata-2 Hydroelectric Power Station is one of the more recent additions to Kyrgyzstan's energy infrastructure along the Naryn River. Although initial construction began in the 1980s, the first phase was only completed in 2010 with the commissioning of a 120-megawatt turbine. A unique feature of the facility is its dam, which was created via a massive, controlled explosion of the adjacent mountainside. The project is closely linked to the much larger planned Kambar-Ata-1, which would drastically increase the nation's energy export capabilities. Kambar-Ata-2 currently helps to reduce the country's reliance on fossil fuels during winter."
